  "concept": {
    "movement": "A compact bronze-and-patina shell moves with a low steady eight-leg wave. Complete pointed feet take clear equal steps; the faster scurry increases cadence and reach without bouncing or stretching the armor.",
    "attack": "The beetle braces its eight feet, pulls its head back, then drives forward into a short armored head-and-mandible shove. Its three real curved jaws flare and clamp while the shell remains whole.",
